    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0577" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg469"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Señor Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 17th instant, and to say that I hastened to bring to the
                    attention of the Secretary of War the telegraphic report which you communicate
                    relative to the alleged assemblage of armed men at San Elizario, Tex., and
                    thereabouts, having designs on the peace of Mexico. I have since received your
                    note of the 19th instant, stating that as you learn from your Government an
                    actual invasion of the Territory of Mexico had already been made by the bandits
                    assembled at the place named, I have accordingly, at once, brought the matter to
                    the notice of the Secretary of War and the Attorney-General.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
